WEBVTT

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.360
<i>Hanamaru Kindergarten</i>

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.330
The Christmas party is tomorrow.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.750
I'm so glad we'll be having a party together.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.780
I know. Why don't we exchange Christmas presents?

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.320
Exchange presents?

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.410
Sounds fun.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:45.430
I'm all for that.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.720
Then we'll do it.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.360
Is that so?

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.940
Yes. I have a Christmas party with my parents every year.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.300
A party with your parents, huh? I suppose I can't do anything about that.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.820
Was there something you wanted to do?

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.510
There's going to be a Christmas party at Anzu-chan's house.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.750
At Anzu-chan's house? That sounds like fun.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.380
Tsuchi must still like Yamamoto-sensei...

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.080
"A Hanamaru Christmas"

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:15.580
I did it!

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.470
Now we just have to cook the chicken, and we'll be ready.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.930
We've got lots of people coming this year, so we'll cook a big one.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.090
Hooray!

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.720
Perfect!

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.920
Anzu, when did Tsuchi and the others say they'd be coming?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.000
Anzu?

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:42.000
Santa, please grant me my wish.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.260
Just this once. Just this one time.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.550
I fell asleep.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.880
Santa granted me my wish!

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.970
I'm an adult woman!

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.650
Wow, I have breasts!

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.010
This could work.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.320
I love you, Anzu-san!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.790
I've got to go show Tsuchi.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.400
Just you wait, Tsuchi!

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.880
My underwear's showing. I need to change.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.660
How wonderful.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:04.290
Wow, thanks for the food!

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.100
Delicious!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.820
Coffee is so bitter.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.590
I'm going to get a present from Santa, too.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.420
You can't.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.330
If you make any detours, we'll run out of time.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.740
Anzu-chan, you've forgotten something important.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.580
Something important?

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.100
It's here.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.550
I'm getting on this?

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.060
Hurry. Get on before Christmas ends.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.180
Before it ends?

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:12.730
You can do it.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.010
Do it.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:16.510
All aboard.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:29.300
Who were those two? I feel like I've met them before.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:35.320
Didn't I come out to the city to meet someone?

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.280
Who am I supposed to meet?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.080
It's someone important, but I can't remember who it is.

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.090
It's snowing.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.750
It's beautiful.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.330
It certainly is beautiful.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.770
It's a wonderful Christmas Eve, miss.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.480
This is the last stop.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.740
Let's go.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:29.880
Okay.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:40.530
I hope I'm not bothering you.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:41.430
Not at all.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.230
I just got the feeling this isn't the first time we've met.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.190
Me, too.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.900
Would it be too much to call this a meeting of destiny?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.320
No, that wouldn't be an exaggeration in the slightest.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.620
My face reaches Tsuchi's.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:53.780
That's right. This man is Tsuchi.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.930
Why had I forgotten?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:05.180
Thank you, Santa, but I have one more wish.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.700
Someday I'd like to actually be with Tsuchi.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.830
Hey, Anzu. Everyone's here.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.090
Anzu-chan's asleep.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:24.050
Aren't we having a Christmas party?

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:29.220
Sorry about that. I'm sure she'll wake up soon.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.220
Senpai, is there anything I can do to help?

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:35.100
Thank you. Could you get the chicken in the kitchen?

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.030
It's huge.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.000
Got it.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.880
Is that Hinagiku-chan?

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.890
Good evening. Thank you for inviting me.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.690
Would it be alright if I stayed for the party, too?

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:55.190
Of course, boss. The more the merrier.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:56.900
Good evening.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.060
Thanks for the invitation.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.340
Welcome. Come on in.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:02.960
Excuse us.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.670
Is Anzu-san alseep?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.570
Come on, Anzu. Everyone's here.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.400
Merry Christmas!

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:20.010
Anzu-chan's father was a teacher at your school?

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:24.660
Yes. At first, it was one-sided on Sakura-senpai's part...

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.240
...but she pursued him aggressively, and they ended up marrying while she was still in school.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:32.310
Married as a student? That's amazing.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.540
I wouldn't expect any less from Anzu-chan's mother.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.400
That sounds like the plot of a drama.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:41.960
She'd flirt with the teacher during lunch. It was unbearable.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.810
Tsuchida-kun, did you have feelings for Anzu-chan's mother?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.150
What? Really?

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:50.630
Did I have feelings for her? Of course not.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:54.050
She was just an energetic kid.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.290
This is my first time in Ginza.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.170
Isn't that it?

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.930
"Hanamaru Feelings"

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.390
Welcome, Tsuchi!

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:11.770
I've never seen so many of my daddy's paintings before.

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:14.370
It's a picture of horses.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:18.300
This is his first show in Japan. Take your time.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.250
Okay.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:24.340
Daddy painted this when we went to America.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.650
I don't really get this stuff.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:36.890
What is it?

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.410
You're in a painting, Anzu-chan.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.850
There's a certain divinity reminiscent of paintings of the mother and child.

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:53.020
The warm colors bring out the warmth of the figures.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.630
You both look wonderful.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:59.510
How embarrassing.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.510
Oh, Tsuchi!

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:03.280
I know I'm cute, but try not to stare too much.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:07.410
It seems you're to thank for this painting, Tsuchi.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.410
What do you mean?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.120
I guess I can tell you.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:28.840
You're from Class B, aren't you?

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:30.110
This painting...

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.350
This painting is absolutely beautiful!

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:37.510
This is a landscape painting of Thailand.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.700
I ended up there after a month of travel.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:45.280
The smell of the windswept fields.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.450
I felt like I'd get sucked into that vast sky.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:51.780
That golden sky gently enveloped the people.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:54.480
It was like a dream.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.250
It really does seem like a dream.

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:02.290
"Members of the Literature Club: Turn in your manuscripts for the Shirakaba Festival by September 15."

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.270
He told me all sorts of stories after that.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:05.840
He's been to lots of other countries, too.

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:07.390
You've already told me that story plenty of times.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:10.030
I'm telling you because I want to tell you about it again.

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:14.260
He knows so many things I don't know.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.770
He's different from other adults.

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:20.930
When I see his paintings, I'm part of his world.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.630
I don't understand art.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.780
There he is.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.280
See you later, Tsuchi.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.090
Guess I'll go home.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.110
When did you get here?

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.500
Just now.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.020
What's wrong?

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.340
He's so far away.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:54.680
Far?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:13:00.500
Even when I try to be part of his world, he's always looking somewhere else.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.880
I can't get close to him.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.010
Senpai...

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.820
Maybe I'm not good enough.

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:10.120
Don't say that.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.000
How do you know you're not good enough?

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:19.470
But...

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:25.250
If you can't enter his world, you should drag him into yours.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.610
Just like you pull me and your friends with you.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:32.490
I'm sure he'll see how you feel. You love him, don't you?

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:38.380
Nothing's stronger than the power of love.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.000
Tsuchi...

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:45.730
If I were worried about something, that's what you'd tell me.

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:49.370
I see. You're right.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.450
I wasn't acting like myself.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.220
Nothing's stronger than the power of love.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.160
That must be true.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.970
It's easy to put effort into something you like.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.950
When it comes to plastic models and games, I...

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.930
Alright, change of plans.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:04.290
I'll be up front with him.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.200
Thanks, Tsuchi.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:15.550
Because of that, I was able to get closer to him, and we eventually married.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.810
Really?

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:22.430
That would make Tsuchida-sensei your Cupid, Sakura-san.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:24.580
Way to go, Tsuchi.

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:29.000
If not for Tsuchi, this painting would never have been made.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.960
You've told me that before, too.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:34.960
About the power of love?

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:40.440
I taught it to you because you love Tsuchi so much.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.750
It's a truly inspiring phrase.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:44.280
I see.

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:45.910
What a wonderful story.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.200
What is it?

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:54.200
Sakura-san got married and had Anzu-chan because of what Tsuchida-kun said...

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:59.930
...and now Anzu-chan is pursuing Tsuchida-kun because of the same words that encouraged her mother.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:01.930
That's true.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:08.910
Oh, I see. Tsuchida-kun's words have returned to him like some kind of boomerang.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:14.450
So Tsuchida-kun has to put up with Anzu-chan because of his own doing.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.850
That's ridiculous.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.830
It's your own doing, Tsuchi.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.920
Looks like you're having fun. What are you talking about?

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:22.620
Daddy.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:25.990
They finally let me out of that formal meeting.

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.290
You must be tired.

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:30.060
You must be tired, too.

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:30.290
In public...

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.660
I'm totally fine.

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.670
That must be nice.

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:36.010
Tsuchida-kun, what do you think of the exhibition?

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:39.200
I don't really understand painting...

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.260
...but that painting.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:44.760
I think that painting is great.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:50.650
I'm sorry. They told us they wanted to rearrange the display.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.780
It's fine. Leave Anzu to us.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:03.940
Look at this snow. I wish I could spend some more time with Yamamoto-sensei.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:05.830
Maybe we could get some tea.

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.820
That was a wonderful story, wasn't it?

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:11.080
About Sakura-senpai?

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:14.940
Yes. It was such a romantic story.

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:22.130
I think it's amazing the words you used to encouraged Sakura-san are inspiring Anzu-chan.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:29.740
We can't see kindness or connections, but those things are everywhere.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:33.400
They are what support our lives.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.060
It's wonderful.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.620
Wonderful, huh?

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:43.160
Wonderful is a great word.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:48.040
I feel like it's the first time I've heard someone say that.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.020
I'll take Anzu back to my place.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.630
Are you sure you'll be able to take care of her?

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:55.750
Yes.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:57.970
Did you wake up?

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.470
Huh? Tsuchi?

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:05.000
Thank you. Good night, Anzu-chan.

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:06.750
Good night.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:10.980
Tsuchida-sensei, let's make tomorrow's party a great one.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:12.310
Of course.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:16.640
Uh, would you like to go to a coffee shop...

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.520
What was that?

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.240
Oh, it's nothing.

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:23.740
Tsuchida-sensei, you don't look well.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.740
Huh? I'm fine. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:29.750
Okay.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.330
Good night.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:32.530
Good night.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:37.770
Hey, Tsuchi.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:42.000
Didn't you want to spend more time with Yamamoto-sensei?

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.750
Don't worry about me. It's fine.

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.160
Why?

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:50.450
"Why?" Yamamoto-sensei and I just aren't meant for each other.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.330
No!

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:56.840
You can't give up!

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:01.740
Don't you love Yamamoto-sensei, Tsuchi?

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.760
If you love her, you can't give up!

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:05.780
What are you talking about?

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:10.530
My mommy said you'll definitely regret it if you give up on someone you love!

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.690
This is messed up. Don't you...

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.510
It's not messed up!

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:20.750
I really love you! I'm going to be your bride!

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:25.320
I want you to be happy, too! That's why you can't give up!

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:26.600
This is too messed up.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:27.990
It's not messed up!

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:29.500
Because...

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:30.770
Because...

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.190
Nothing's stronger than the power of love!

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:42.020
I guess I can't back down if you say that.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:45.220
I'll confess my feelings to her again.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:46.390
Tsuchi...

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:03.780
That's right. We don't have to be perfect for each other.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:07.230
It's okay if I'm pathetic. I am who I am.

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:10.250
I love Yamamoto-sensei.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:15.170
My drunken confession didn't work out, but I'm sober this time!

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:18.060
You can do it, Tsuchi!

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:18.970
Alright!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:25.380
Yamamoto-sensei!

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:27.790
Yamamoto-sensei!

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.820
Are you alright?

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.090
I'm fine.

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:37.860
More importantly, there's something I want to tell you.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:39.540
Tell me?

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.270
I'm only half a man.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:49.390
Compared to you, I'm immature.

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:50.680
But...

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.230
But...

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.520
But when I become a real man, will you...

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.750
That's not true.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:02.090
You're doing a great job even though you've only been at the kindergarten for a year.

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.490
There's no way you're only half a man.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:08.540
Thank you, but I'm trying to say...

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:11.690
Is that what you were depressed about?

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:15.230
I'm trying to be more like you, Tsuchida-sensei.

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:19.660
I'd like to play with the children the way you do.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:21.000
Is that so?

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:29.580
I thought I might get along with the children better if I played games like you, but I'm no good at them.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:33.710
You play games? You don't need to do that.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.130
Today isn't Tsuchi's day, either.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.700
That's right.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:46.470
Tsuchi tried to confess his feelings for Yamamoto-sensei, but she thought he was talking about work.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.760
I had heard Yamamoto-sensei is a late bloomer, but I didn't think it could be that bad.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.780
Tsuchi's got his work cut out for him.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.150
He really does.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.870
Being an adult sounds hard.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:59.000
I don't think this problem comes from being an adult.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:07.970
Anzu-chan's decision to support Tsuchida-sensei's love will create an awfully complicated relationship.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.930
The party's about to start.

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.210
We're starting with a puppet show.

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.180
It's a story Tsuchida-sensei made up.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:20.050
A giant panda-cat suddenly appeared in the Fairy Tale Kingdom and went on a violent rampage.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:22.160
The princess was worried.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:26.450
What am I going to do? The Fairy Tale Kingdom is in a panic.

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.760
Don't worry, princess.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:31.070
You're the prince from the neighboring kingdom.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:34.610
I made a giant robot for just this kind of situation.

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:36.420
Hanamaru Robot, go!

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:40.900
What's a robot doing in a fairy tale?

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.550
Men love robots.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:44.810
This is great. They love it.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:46.370
Amazing, Tsuchida-sensei.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.120
You can do it.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:50.650
What an original story.

00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:51.670
You can do it, Tsuchi.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.530
Hanamaru Punch!

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:56.200
I'm done for! Please, forgive me!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:56.930
Are you sure?

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:34.450
"Thank you!"
